# UI font size default

Sidebar body text uses `text-nav` (16px / Lexend). That is the **minimum** size for UI work in this app.

When adding or changing UI:

- Use `font-sans text-nav font-ui` for labels, buttons, inputs, table headers/cells, placeholders, helper text, dialog body, and nav-like copy.
- Do **not** default to `text-sm` (14px) or `text-xs` (12px) for normal UI text.
- Prefer matching existing sidebar patterns over inventing smaller type.
- `text-sm` / `text-xs` only for rare dense metadata when the user explicitly asks for smaller type.

Token reference (`frontend/src/design/tokens.ts`):

- `nav`: 16px — default UI
- `base`: 16px — same size, slightly taller line-height
- `sm` / `xs`: too small for default UI; avoid
